 "brief": {
  "short_answer": "Yes. The ASRS-like report notes loss of controller link and attempts to use RTH, but RTH did not engage as expected, aligning with documented loss-of-link responses and predefined RTH behavior described in FAA guidance and the DJI Matrice 210 manual.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "section": "faa",
    "label": "FAA guidance",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "Loss of control link triggers emergency or contingency procedures, including attempting to reestablish the link and, if unsuccessful, initiating loss-of-control procedures such as RTH.",
      "citations": [
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0228",
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0227",
       "dji_m210_v1_manual_v14_c0037"
      ],
      "quote": "If connection cannot be reestablished, start emergency or contingency procedures for loss of control link.",
      "conditions": [
       "Loss of control link occurs"
      ],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C001",
      "section": "faa",
      "tier": "official",
      "incident_label": null
     },
     {
      "text": "The remote PIC may initiate a return-to-home sequence as part of loss-of-link or failsafe procedures; if VLOS is lost, the manual instructs to follow pre-determined procedures, which may include RTH.",
      "citations": [
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0049",
       "dji_m210_v1_manual_v14_c0037"
      ],
      "quote": "For example, the remote PIC may need to land the small unmanned aircraft immediately, enter hover mode, or employ a return-to-home sequence.",
